    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-opening-bala-kanda-006",
      "sequence": 6,
      "meaning": "I revere Hari, the sovereign named Rāma, supreme cause of all: the entire universe, including gods beginning with Brahmā and the demons, moves under his māyā; by his reality everything unreal appears real, like the illusion of a snake in a rope; and his foot alone is the boat for those who wish to cross the ocean of becoming.",
      "sourceRef": "Belvedere Press 1925 facsimile, scan page 53",
      "sourceUrl": "https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.342236/page/n52/mode/1up",
      "note": "Original close English rendering of the pinned edition-specific reading; editorial work awaiting independent review.",
