    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-opening-bala-kanda-007",
      "sequence": 7,
      "meaning": "For the delight of his own heart, Tulasī unfolds this exceedingly lovely composition in the vernacular on the story of Raghunātha, drawing on what is approved by many Purāṇas, Vedas and Āgamas, what is told in the Rāmāyaṇa, and occasionally what comes from elsewhere.",
